Hello guys 👋 Today we’re kicking off the first session in my Java learning series.
don’t overlook simple examples as they may look small, but they build the foundation we need to understand bigger and more complex programs later on.
📝 The Program


Here’s the simplest Java program we’ll be looking at:
public class FirstSample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Hello, World!");
    }
}


Keywords You Should Understand Before Continuing
JVM (Java Virtual Machine):
The JVM is like the heart of Java. When you write Java code, it doesn’t run directly on your computer’s hardware. Instead, it’s compiled into bytecode (a universal form of code). The JVM’s job is to read and execute this bytecode on any machine.
